  "problems": "",
  "rationale": "Setting skip_markduplicates to true bypasses the entire BAM_MARKDUPLICATES_PICARD subworkflow, causing downstream quality control, StringTie and coverage-generation processes to consume the original sorted BAM files and their indices instead of duplicate-marked BAM files. MultiQC receives alignment statistics directly from ALIGN_STAR rather than BAM_MARKDUPLICATES_PICARD, together with the regenerated downstream QC outputs and without Picard duplication metrics. STAR alignment, transcriptome-based Salmon quantification, independent pseudo-alignment and their associated DESeq2 analyses remain unaffected because their computational inputs and commands do not depend on the duplicate-marking branch."
